#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalcul; is a math application for young children (starting age 6) testing "
"them on additions, substractions, multiplications and divisions. Two kinds "
"of exercises can be done with kalcul: tests on operations where you set the "
"operation type and the range and then the program asks random numbers "
"questions and preset levels where you set yourself the questions asked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalcul; aims to be simple to use for the child but powerful enough to leave "
"plenty of options and settings for the adult (parent or teacher). &kalcul; "
"also saves the result of any test in a file associated to the current "
"username and we plan to make those results available through KSpread and "
"KChart (or any other office application)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kalcul;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalcul; main window consists of the text area on the left and the timer on "
"the right. The timer is a clock which either times your test or tells you to "
"take a test in a given amount of time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &kalcul; main window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalcul; main window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the Start button to start a test. The clock starts and a question is "
"displayed. This is the Practice Mode where questions are randomly chosen and "
"some parameters can be chosen in the <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> -&gt; "
"<guimenuitem>Exercise Dialog</guimenuitem> menu. Defaults are: the operation "
"is addition with two terms and each term is lower than 10."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Start a test</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Start a test</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click the <guibutton>Stop</guibutton> button then the test is stopped "
"and everything is reset to begin a new test."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click the <guibutton>Pause</guibutton> button, the test is switched "
"in Pause mode, the question remains displayed, the timer is paused. Clicking "
"the <guibutton>Continue</guibutton> button will resume the test."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Two progress bars shows you how many questions you answered so far and how "
"many answers were correct."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Feedback</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Feedback</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the statusbar are displayed the user name, the number of correct answers "
"and the number of questions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "When a test is finished, a result dialog displays the tests results."
msgstr ""

